(:id "port/squirrel/fixed/numeric-evolution" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/squirreltable/fixed_evolution_proof_test.go: TestSquirrelFixedEvolutionNumericWidening") :tested-revision "8241dad00d55bd7e4ac078a398b4ba09569bfd41" :note "2026-11-07: E3, C8, R20, R21 under strict-only: a compiled plan widens int16 to int32 sign-extended and float32 to float64 exactly, lands an appended field's default, and counts widened once per leaf per record; the identity plan widens nothing. The writer's range governs a compiled read: 150 inside the reader's [0, 200] and outside the writer's [0, 100] refuses out_of_range, scalar and fixed-array element (emitter fix: lineage entries carry the writer's ranges). Files are framed from the compiler's own layout and hash (FixedLineageOf) or written by the emitted FixedSave; each runtime rule's negative control plants a break into the emitted module and the row goes red. Run on the studio (Darwin arm64) at 8241dad00 with the pinned Squirrel 3.2 and SCHEMA_SLOW=1; CI re-runs it on Linux.")
(:id "port/squirrel/fixed/reports" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/squirreltable/fixed_evolution_proof_test.go: TestSquirrelFixedEvolutionReports") :tested-revision "8241dad00d55bd7e4ac078a398b4ba09569bfd41" :note "2026-11-07: E9, R16, R18 under strict-only: widened is the one counter; every load resets FixedWidened, FixedReason and FixedField, so a widening file reads w4 on every load and a clean load after a refusal names no reason; an append the reader knows is not an event; a range filling its width cannot fire over 256 records; no clamp, duplicate, kind-mismatch or unknown counter is carried. Files are framed from the compiler's own layout and hash (FixedLineageOf) or written by the emitted FixedSave; each runtime rule's negative control plants a break into the emitted module and the row goes red. Run on the studio (Darwin arm64) at 8241dad00 with the pinned Squirrel 3.2 and SCHEMA_SLOW=1; CI re-runs it on Linux.")
(:id "port/squirrel/fixed/scalar-bounds" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/squirreltable/fixed_evolution_proof_test.go: TestSquirrelFixedEvolutionScalarBounds") :tested-revision "8241dad00d55bd7e4ac078a398b4ba09569bfd41" :note "2026-11-07: C7, R30 under strict-only: ranged int32, int128, uint16 and uint64 land at both ends and refuse out_of_range one past either end, compared in the field's own type (int128 by its high word, uint64 at 2^63 + 7 unsigned); a compressed float is saved as its float32 bits, refused outside its range, and a finer or dropped resolution moves the hash and reads the old bits unchanged (emitter fix: int128 and uint128 ranges were never checked). Files are framed from the compiler's own layout and hash (FixedLineageOf) or written by the emitted FixedSave; each runtime rule's negative control plants a break into the emitted module and the row goes red. Run on the studio (Darwin arm64) at 8241dad00 with the pinned Squirrel 3.2 and SCHEMA_SLOW=1; CI re-runs it on Linux.")
(:id "port/squirrel/fixed/ordinals" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/squirreltable/fixed_evolution_proof_test.go: TestSquirrelFixedEvolutionOrdinals") :tested-revision "8241dad00d55bd7e4ac078a398b4ba09569bfd41" :note "2026-11-07: C9, C10, R31 under strict-only: an enum ordinal past the writer's variants and a union tag past its arms refuse out_of_range on the identity plan and on a compiled plan whose reader declares more (the writer's count governs); zero lands None; 300-variant enums and 300-arm unions ride two-byte ordinals (emitter fix: compiled plans landed None or the reader's appended variant). Files are framed from the compiler's own layout and hash (FixedLineageOf) or written by the emitted FixedSave; each runtime rule's negative control plants a break into the emitted module and the row goes red. Run on the studio (Darwin arm64) at 8241dad00 with the pinned Squirrel 3.2 and SCHEMA_SLOW=1; CI re-runs it on Linux.")
